# No trailing slash: a directory-only pattern misses a SYMLINK named
# node_modules, which an agent worktree may create. Git then stages it, and a
# fresh CI clone dies in `pnpm install` with `ENOTDIR: not a directory, mkdir
# .../node_modules`. Keep this bare so both the real directory and a symlink
# are ignored.
node_modules
dist/
out/
build/
.nx/cache
.nx/workspace-data
.vite/
.astro/
*.log
.DS_Store
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
.env
.env.local
release/
tmp
**/__pycache__

# Storybook
storybook-static/

# Vitest browser mode writes these only when a test FAILS — a screenshot of the
# page and the attachments that go with it. They are debugging output for the
# run that produced them, worthless to anyone else, and without this a red run
# leaves untracked files sitting in `git status` waiting to be swept into
# someone's `git add -A`.
.vitest-attachments/
**/__screenshots__/

.claude/worktrees
.claude/**/.eval-labs
.claude/**/.state
# Plan files are local-only resume aids (see CLAUDE.md > Development Workflow) — never committed
.claude/plans/
# Single-use gate tokens (pipeline spec §7) — the durable record is frontmatter status + date
.claude/gate-tokens/

.nx/polygraph
.nx/self-healing
.nx/migrate-runs
target/
